      "writtenOn": "2019-01-21T08:10:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please be specific.\nIn Python 0 is false and every other integer is true.\nIn Ruby all integers are true, including 0.\nIn Java and Kotlin integers are not truth values.\nIn C it\u0027s all over the place. errno has 0 for success, as has strcmp, but if (0) is false and if (1) is true.\n\nSo which is it here ?\n\nWhatever you are used to, you can bet other programmers have a different experience. This is especially true here in Java where integers are not truth values.\n\nIf you don\u0027t mind, also please update the doc for the two methods above.",
