      "writtenOn": "2019-01-21T08:10:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you comment on the rationale of closing this fd ? ISTM the implementation here doesn\u0027t necessarily own the fd and it\u0027s not necessarily expected the TCP connection is closed for the client – especially since here there is no programmatic way for the client to tell.\n\nSo two issues :\n・Does this implementation own the FD ? If not let\u0027s not close the FD for them. Possibly let the exception bubble up or something.\n・Is it impossible one received packet is malformed but we still want to continue listening ? Suppose there is a bug in the implementation of the DNS server, might we not want to still continue proxying its queries/replies ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 329,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 329,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "8de990c5dca373c2c0577465ed752646a5548c64",
